      "role": "user",
      "content": "i see. so you're saying that if someone's argument is based on \"unproven conspiracy theories\" or \"pseudo-science,\" it doesn't really count as a legitimate concern anymore? it feels like that kind of framing might lead students to just dismiss any argument that challenges the government's side as \"misinformation\" by default. shouldn't the debate be about whether the government's actions are justified, regardless of the scientific consensus?",
